# Copy this file to `server/.env`, then fill in one provider key.
#
#   cp server/.env.example server/.env
#   chmod 600 server/.env
#   $EDITOR server/.env
#
# Docker Compose reads `server/.env` automatically, and the compose file passes
# the whole file into the container. Never commit `server/.env`.
#
# Model providers
# ---------------
# DS Bot is not tied to one provider. Model routes come from DSH's
# @deepseek-ai/dsh-llm-pi-ai adapter, and each route names the environment
# variable that holds its key (`apiKeyEnv`). The variable name here must match
# that route.
#
# The bundled compose is written for an OpenCode Go route. That is one option,
# not a requirement: add a route for another provider to the container profile
# and put its key here under the same name. More: docs/providers.md.
OPENCODE_GO_API_KEY=

# Common alternatives. Leave them commented unless the profile declares a route
# with that apiKeyEnv.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=

# Optional: container user and group. Compose defaults to 1000:1000.
# PUID=1000
# PGID=1000

# Optional: instance identity and host paths. Defaults shown. Override them to
# run more than one compose instance, or to keep data outside /opt. Keep
# DS_BOT_PORT out of 13090-13199, which the hub uses for browser origins.
# DS_BOT_CONTAINER=ds-bot
# DS_BOT_PORT=13081
# DS_BOT_DATA_DIR=/opt/ds-bot/data
# DS_BOT_WORKSPACE_DIR=/opt/ds-bot/workspace
